# Purpose/owner: reliability.capacity_configuration selects the isolated read-only
# workload JSON for monitoring_capacity.py; type absolute canonical regular path.
# Default: tracked capacity.json when neither CLI nor --workload-env-file is given.
# Values/ranges/units: capacity.schema.json; no URL, customer PID or secret accepted.
# Secret handling: nonsecret policy only; actual sessions remain fixture memory and
# reports live in the centrally owned private evidence directory. No secret value.
# Precedence/mapping: --workload-configuration overrides this exact one key from
# --workload-env-file; otherwise tracked default. Unknown/duplicate/empty keys fail.
# No direct process environment reads; wrapper injects validated test-only input/
# output paths into its exact new test binary. Compose/Helm is not used for this
# local quality profile. New run required after changes; no reload or daemon.
PROJECT_ONE_MONITORING_CAPACITY_CONFIG_FILE=/run/projectone/validation/monitoring-capacity.json
